# Scripted events for the "dips" recording (dips on single notes, then on chords), in ms on the
# recording's clock. The first part transposes while notes are held, then returns to no transposition.
# The second holds Switch 1, assigned to Sustain, across the chord dips, and the last line queries a
# setting by NRPN.

setting footRight transposeUp          # the switches these events use; the others keep their defaults
setting footLeft transposeDown
setting switch1 sustain

48500   press footRight                # Transpose Up, a note held (47.85-54.6 s)
48700   release footRight
82000   press footRight                # Transpose Up again, a note held (81.15-86 s)
82300   release footRight
130500  press footLeft                 # Transpose Down, twice: back to no transposition (a note held, 129.65-136.6 s)
130800  release footLeft
131500  press footLeft
131800  release footLeft

206000  press switch1                  # Switch 1 held as a sustain pedal: down with three or more notes held (205.25-209.1 s)
216000  release switch1                # up with three or more notes held (214.35-218 s)

219000  nrpn 299 261                   # query: Global MIDI CC For Switch 1 Sustain
